<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cen Chunxuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cen Chunxuan was a late Qing official who served as governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> and of Liangguang. In the early Republic he opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>, and from 1918 he chaired the directorate of the military government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a> generals forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen</a> out. His government collapsed in 1920, and he retired from politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cen-chunxuan.jpg" alt="Cen Chunxuan" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B2%91%E6%98%A5%E7%85%8A.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
